		(property "Sourcing_Note" "Was a 500R damping resistor when the ring ran at Vdrive. Now the upper leg of a divider: the last LED in the chain swings its DOUT to 5V, which must not reach the main board's 3.3V domain. 2.2k/3.9k gives 3.20V at the connector. It still damps the return line at its source end, which is what the 500R was for."
			(at 50.8 105.41 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
