					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Sourcing_Note" "Boosts the cable's Vdrive (battery, 3.0-4.2V) to the 5.0V the Inolux LEDs are specified at. Values follow datasheet Figure 8-1, the Li-ion to 5V reference: 10uF in, 2x22uF out, 732k/100k feedback divider. Vref 0.595V typ gives Vout = 0.595 x (1 + 732/100) = 4.95V. Inductor is 2.2uH rather than the reference 1uH - still inside the datasheet's 0.37-2.9uH range - to halve the ripple current next to the GNSS and LoRa antennas. Chosen partly for its true input-to-output disconnect in shutdown, which is what lets RING_EN kill the 16 LEDs' 8mA static draw."
			(at 91.44 163.83 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
