				)
			)
		)
		(property "Sourcing_Note" "Level shifter for NEOPIX. Mandatory at 5V: the Inolux part specifies V_IH = 3.4V minimum at VDD = 5.0V, which 3.3V logic cannot meet. AHCT is the right family because its TTL thresholds (V_IH 2.0V at VCC 5V) accept a 3.3V input directly. OE is tied low so the buffer is always enabled. When RING_EN is low the 5V rail is down and the MCU must hold NEOPIX low too, or it will forward-bias this input's ESD clamp - the main board's 500R series damping resistor limits that to a few mA, but it is a firmware rule."
			(at 148.59 39.37 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
